            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Latin for a crime against heaven, then the Latin for unfair."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: castīgō, castīgāre",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "castīgō, castīgāre — \"to punish, to correct; to rebuke\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Pater fīlium verbīs castīgāvit. The father rebuked his son."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "castīgō, castīgāre, castīgāvī, castīgātum, built on castus, pure: to set right. English castigate and chastise."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "castīgō is built on castus \"pure\" (EtymDB; Lewis & Short): to set a person right. English castigate and chastise come from it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
